# 007 · Known limits and the security model

**Status:** `READY` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Tester basics

## What

A docs page on what Thermite does not do yet, and what a tester must know before running it:

- agents run code that a model wrote, on your machine;
- under compose, that code can reach your local network;
- there are no default caps, so set a stop time or a budget before you use a paid key;
- RunPod GPUs are shared machines, so timing is noisier there;
- research mode has no web search yet;
- multi-day runs are not yet proven;
- 0.x versions make no upgrade promise.

With it, a short security model: what each part can reach and what it trusts.

## Why

Testers must know the risks before they start.

## Done when

- [ ] The page exists and is linked from the quick start and the README.
- [ ] Each limit links to the goal that removes it.

